## 3. Configure for your infrastructure

Everything site-specific is in the files below. The roles contain no site values.

### 3.1 Decide your values first

Fill this in before editing files:

| Value | Your value | Goes into |
|---|---|---|
| Proxmox node names (exactly as `pvecm nodes` shows them) and their IPs | | `hosts.yml`, `host_vars`, `proxmox.yml` |
| Proxmox API host | | `proxmox.yml` |
| Template VM ID, template node | | `proxmox.yml` |
| VM storage ID (exact case), ISO storage ID and its path | | `proxmox.yml` |
| Proxmox pool name | | `proxmox.yml`, section 4 |
| Bridge, VLAN tag (if any) | | `network.yml` |
| Per env: 3 VM names, 3 VM IDs, 3 IPs, VIP, VRRP ID | | `environments.yml`, `hosts.yml`, `host_vars` |
| Subnet prefix, gateway, DNS, search domain | | `network.yml` |
| Admin CIDRs (must contain the workstation) and app CIDRs | | `network.yml` |
| Prometheus server IP | | `environments.yml` |
| VM sizing: vCPU, RAM, OS disk + LV sizes, pgdata/pgwal/pgaudit sizes | | `main.yml` |
| SSH public key file | | `proxmox.yml` |

### 3.2 Environment registry: `playbooks/group_vars/all/environments.yml`

This registry is the single source of truth for addresses of **all** environments. Each environment's firewall and hba rules reject every other environment's IPs from here, so keep all environments in it, even ones not deployed yet.

```yaml
pgc_environments:
  [[ env ]]:
    nodes:                                   # VM name: IP. Names must equal the inventory host names.
[% for n in nodes %]
      [[ n.name ]]: [[ n.ip ]]
[% endfor %]
    vip: [[ vip ]]
    keepalived_vrid: [[ vrid ]][[ ' ' * (24 - (vrid|string|length)) ]]# unique per env on the L2 segment
    vm_ids: [[ vm_ids | list ]][[ ' ' * (33 - (vm_ids|list|string|length)) ]]# the only VM IDs provisioning may touch for this env
[% for o in others %]
  [[ o ]]:                                   # keep it: [[ env ]]'s firewall and hba reject its addresses
    ...
[% endfor %]
pgc_reserved_ips:                        # IPs that must never be assigned, e.g. ones other machines use
[% for ip in reserved_ips %]
  - [[ ip ]]
[% endfor %]
prometheus_server_ip: [[ prometheus_ip ]]                     # only this IP may scrape metrics
```

The environment key (`[[ env ]]`) must equal `pgc_env` in `inventories/[[ env ]]/group_vars/all/main.yml`.

### 3.3 Hosts: `inventories/[[ env ]]/hosts.yml`

- `pve_nodes`: your Proxmox node names with their IPs, used for SSH to the template node.
- `pg_nodes`: the three VM names with `ansible_host` IPs, identical to the registry.

The group name `pgc_[[ env ]]` is free text.

### 3.4 Per VM: `inventories/[[ env ]]/host_vars/<vm-name>.yml`

```yaml
# [[ nodes[0].name ]]
vm_id: [[ nodes[0].vm_id ]]                 # must be in the registry's vm_ids for this env
vm_pve_node: [[ nodes[0].pve_node ]]     # Proxmox node that hosts this VM; the three VMs must be on three different nodes
keepalived_priority: 100   # 100 / 90 / 80: highest gets the VIP first
```

**Node names must be the real Proxmox node names** (`pvecm nodes`, column `Name`, case-sensitive) in `vm_pve_node`, `pve_template_node` and the `pve_nodes` hosts of `hosts.yml`. They are passed to the Proxmox API and used in the HA rules; this environment uses [[ nodes | map(attribute='pve_node') | join(', ') ]].

### 3.5 Sizing: `inventories/[[ env ]]/group_vars/all/main.yml`

| Variable | [[ env ]] | Rules |
|---|---|---|
| `pgc_env` | `[[ env ]]` | Key in the registry |
| `vm_cores`, `vm_memory_mb` | [[ main.vm_cores ]], [[ main.vm_memory_mb ]] | RAM also sets `shared_buffers` (25 %) and `effective_cache_size` (75 %) |
| `vm_os_disk_gb` | [[ main.vm_os_disk_gb ]] | At least 20 (template disk). Must hold 1 GB `/boot` plus the sum of `vm_os_lvm`. |
| `vm_os_lvm` | [% for l in main.vm_os_lvm %][[ l.lv ]] [[ l.size_gb ]][[ ', ' if not loop.last ]][% endfor %] | Sizes in GB. LVs are only grown, never shrunk. |
| `vm_pg_disks[].size_gb` | [% for d in main.vm_pg_disks %][[ d.name ]] [[ d.size_gb ]][[ ', ' if not loop.last ]][% endfor %] | Keep the names, slots, VG/LV names and mounts as they are |
| `patroni_synchronous_mode` | [[ sync_mode | string | lower ]] | true: a commit waits for one replica, so no committed transaction is lost on failover. Non-strict: writes continue if no replica is up. Takes effect at the first bootstrap only; later use `patronictl edit-config`. |
| `patroni_watchdog_mode` | [[ watchdog ]] | required: a node whose watchdog doesn't work never becomes leader |

Provisioning refuses to run while any of these is empty.

